@title CRM selection for Hartwell Industrial Supply
@subtitle 140 sales and account-management seats, three shortlisted vendors

Our sales operations lead is choosing a CRM for 140 sales and account-management seats. We scored each vendor from 1 to 5 against five weighted criteria.

## Scorecard

data scores = criterion,weight %,Pipeboard,Cardinal CRM,Thistle; Fit to our workflow,30,4,5,3; Integration with our ERP,25,5,3,4; Cost,20,3,2,5; Admin effort,15,4,3,3; Support quality,10,4,5,3; Weighted total,100,4.05,3.60,3.65

table scores title="Scores from 1 to 5, with weights"

## Annual license cost

At list prices, 140 seats cost:

data cost = vendor,list price per seat per month,annual cost; Pipeboard,65,109200; Cardinal CRM,89,149520; Thistle,42,70560

chart hbar cost y=annual cost unit=$ labels title="Annual license cost for 140 seats"

Thistle is the cheapest, at $70,560 a year. Cardinal CRM is the most expensive, at $149,520 a year.

## Risks

- **Pipeboard.** The ERP connector is certified, but the vendor is a 2019 startup.
- **Cardinal CRM.** Best fit for our workflow, but it needs a 12-week implementation and a partner.
- **Thistle.** Cheapest, but its reporting is weak, and two of our dashboards would have to be rebuilt elsewhere.

## Recommendation

We go with Pipeboard, pending a reference call with another industrial distributor, scheduled for 2026-10-28. Pipeboard has the highest weighted total, at 4.05, and costs $109,200 a year at list price. The reference call is the check that could change this decision.
